<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3185] Hadoop: Improve Hadoop JAR search logic.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3185</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Problem&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Currently our &lt;tt&gt;HadoopClassLoader&lt;/tt&gt; is trying to find common/hdfs/mapred JARs automatically if &lt;tt&gt;HADOOP_HOME&lt;/tt&gt; is set. However, it checks only for standard Apache Hadoop distribution paths (/share/hadoop/*). For other distributions (CDH, HDP), user has to bother with additional env variables manually.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Solution&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Try to search for the following folders as well:&lt;br/&gt;
$HADOOP_HOME/hadoop&lt;br/&gt;
$HADOOP_HOME/hadoop-hdfs&lt;br/&gt;
$HADOOP_HOME/hadoop-mapreduce&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If all these folders are found, then this is either HDP or CDH deployment and we can create the classpath without additional env vars.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
